#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:69 imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:429
#: imageplugin_noisereduction.cpp:63
msgid "Noise Reduction"
msgstr "Reduzón de Ruído"

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:71
#, fuzzy
msgid "A noise reduction image filter plugin for digiKam."
msgstr "Un plugin de digiKam para reducir o ruído da imaxe."

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:77
msgid "Author and maintainer"
msgstr "Autoria e mantimento"

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:80
#, fuzzy
msgid "Original Noise Reduction algorithm author"
msgstr "Autor do algoritmo de reduzón de ruído do Gimp"

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:91
msgid "Details"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:93
msgid "Radius:"
msgstr "Rádio:"

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:98
msgid ""
"<p><b>Radius</b>: this control selects the gliding window size used for the "
"filter. Larger values increase the amount of time needed to filter each pixel "
"in the image and can cause blurring. This window moves across the image, and "
"the color in it is smoothed to remove imperfections. In any case it must be "
"about the same size as noise granularity or somewhat more. If it is set higher "
"than necessary, then it can cause unwanted blur."
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:112
msgid "Texture:"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:117
msgid ""
"<p><b>Texture</b>: this control set the texture accuracy. This value can be "
"used, to get more or less texture accuracy. When decreased, then noise and "
"texture are blurred out, when increased then texture is amplified, but also "
"noise will increase. It has almost no effect to image edges, opposed to filter "
"<b>Edge</b>, which would blur edges, when increased. If <b>Edge</b> "
"is adjusted in away so that edges are sharp, and there is still too much area "
"noise, then texture detail could be used to reduce noise without blurring "
"edges. Another way would be to decrease <b>Radius</b> and to increase <b>"
"Edge</b>."
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:132
msgid "Sharpness:"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:137
msgid ""
"<p><b>Sharpness</b>: this control set the sharpness level. This value defines "
"the pixel distance in which the filter looks ahead for luminance variations. "
"When this value is increased, then spikenoise is erased. You can eventually "
"readjust filter <b>Edge</b>, when you changed this setting. When this value is "
"to high, then the adaptive filter cannot longer accurately track image details, "
"and noise can reappear or blur can occur."
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:149
msgid "Edge:"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:154
msgid ""
"<p><b>Edge</b>: this control set the edge accuracy for sharpness. This value "
"improves the frequency response for the filter. When it is too strong then not "
"all noise can be removed, or spike noise may appear. Set it near to maximum, if "
"you want to remove weak noise or JPEG-artifacts, without loosing detail."
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:166
msgid "Erosion:"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:171
msgid ""
"<p><b>Erosion</b>: this control set the phase shift for edges. This value can "
"be used to erodes singular spikes and it has a smooth effect to edges, and "
"sharpens edges by erosion, so noise at edges is eroded. The effect is dependant "
"from <b>Sharpness</b>, <b>Damping</b>, and <b>Edges</b>"
". Set it to minimum, if you want to remove weak noise or JPEG-artifacts. When "
"this value is increased, then also increasing <b>Damping</b> "
"is often useful. This setting can provides sharpening and antialiasing effect "
"to edges when spike noise is corrected."
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:189
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:191
msgid "Luminance:"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:196
msgid ""
"<p><b>Luminance</b>: this control set the luminance tolerance of image. It's "
"recommended to use only <b>Color</b> or <b>Luminance</b> "
"tolerance settings to make an image correction, not the both at the same time. "
"This settings don't influence the main smoothing process controled by <b>"
"Details</b> settings."
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:206
msgid "Threshold:"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:211
msgid ""
"<p><b>Threshold</b>: this control set the 2nd derivative of luminance "
"adjustment. This value should be set so that edges are clearly visible and "
"noise is smoothed out. This value is not bound to any intensity value, it is "
"bound to the second derivative of intensity values. Simply adjust it and watch "
"the preview. Adjustment must be made carefully, because the gap between "
"\"noisy\", \"smooth\", and \"blur\" is very small. Adjust it as carefully as "
"you would adjust the focus of a camera."
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:224
msgid "Color:"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:229
msgid ""
"<p><b>Color</b>: this control set the color tolerance of image. It's "
"recommended to use only <b>Color</b> or <b>Luminance</b> "
"tolerance settings to make an image correction, not the both at the same time. "
"This settings don't influence the main smoothing process controled by <b>"
"Details</b> settings."
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:239
msgid "Gamma:"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:244
msgid ""
"<p><b>Gamma</b>: this control set the gamma tolerance of image. This value can "
"be used to increase the tolerance values for darker areas (which commonly are "
"more noisy). This results in more blur for shadow areas."
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:253
msgid "Damping:"
msgstr ""

#: imageeffect_noisereduction.cpp:258
msgid ""
"<p><b>Damping</b>: this control set the phase jitter damping adjustement. This "
"value defines how fast the adaptive filter-radius reacts to luminance "
"variations. If increased, then edges appear smoother, if too high, then blur "
"may occur. If at minimum then noise and phase jitter at edges can occur. It can "
"supress spike noise when increased and this is the preferred method to remove "
"it."
msgstr ""

